.TH USB-STORAGE-WATCH 8 "October 2026" "USB Storage Watch 2.0.0~ui6"
.SH NAME
usb-storage-watch \- monitor one ext4 filesystem with optional guarded recovery
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B usb-storage-watch
.RI [ --version ]
.RI [ --root " directory" ]
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
Monitors the configured ext4 filesystem and records persistent incidents.
Normal mounts, qualified individual USB port recovery and selected Docker
container recovery require explicit configuration. Installation does not
enable or start the service. No formatting or filesystem repair is performed.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Interactively select storage and optional recovery/notification settings.
Stop the service before changing configuration.
.TP
.B smtp-setup
Configure authenticated SMTP with verified STARTTLS or implicit TLS.
.TP
.B validate
Validate protected configuration without printing credentials.
.TP
.B diagnose
Check configuration, persistent state, dependencies and current mount health.
.TP
.B check
Print current filesystem observations. Exit 2 means storage is unhealthy.
.TP
.B status
Print private persistent incident, recovery and delivery information.
.TP
.B test-email
Send one explicitly labelled test to the configured SMTP recipient.
.TP
.B verify-apps
Check selected Docker binds and running-container access without restarting.
.TP
.B run
Run the monitor. Normally invoked through usb-storage-watch.service.
.TP
.B usb-candidate --output PATH
Collect private hardware identity without qualifying or resetting a port.
.TP
.B qualify-usb --profile PATH --date YYYY-MM-DD --evidence TEXT
Record operator attestation of an independent offline qualification.
Unsupported or unqualified hardware must retain USB recovery disabled.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --root DIRECTORY
Use a staged installation for validate or diagnose only; no host probes.
.TP
.B --version
Print the distribution version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/usb-storage-watch/config.json
Root-owned configuration, mode 0600 in a mode 0700 directory.
.TP
.I /etc/usb-storage-watch/smtp.json
Root-owned SMTP credentials with the same protections.
.TP
.I /var/lib/usb-storage-watch
Private persistent state, retained on removal and purge.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/usb-storage-watch/README.md
Installation instructions, recovery scope and links to detailed documentation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR fstab (5)
